Cell[TextData[{
 "The segment graph contains all shortest paths from ",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 " to ",
 StyleBox["q", "TI"],
 ", oriented toward ",
 StyleBox["q", "TI"],
 ". A central vertex minimizes Max[d(p,v),d(v,q)] within this graph. Even \
endpoint distance gives one middle layer; odd distance gives both middle \
layers. Disconnected endpoints give an empty family; equal anchors give one \
point. Sampling is uniform over distinct central vertices. The InfraMidpoint \
\"VertexDensity\" measurement separately counts shortest-path occupation at \
each center."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"36ac8f2a-a95b-4743-9e00-dcf27fee3a02"],

Cell["\<\
The graph must be finite, simple, undirected and unweighted, with valid \
anchors. Omitted count or Automatic gives one uniformly random vertex; an \
empty pool gives {}. An integer gives that many distinct vertices, or {} when \
too few exist. UpTo[n] gives at most n distinct vertices; All gives the \
complete pool in graph vertex order. Zero gives {}; negative counts and \
unsupported options stay unevaluated.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"e535052c-4a62-43ee-89a7-aeeb98a3bf41"],

Cell["\<\
\"NextVertexFunction\" defaults to Automatic. Identity selects in graph \
vertex order. These are the only supported selector values. All and Identity \
do not advance random state. List-valued points remain intact. For an \
empty-List vertex, All and count 1 distinguish {{}} from an empty pool.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"c34132b8-686d-4c76-b45e-8772aa268a48"]
}, Open  ]],

